A large university hospital has a team of 35 medical specialists comprising of cardiologist, oncologist and neurologists. The breakdown reveals that 12 specialists focus on cardiology, 9 specialise on oncology and 6 specialise in neurology. Notably 5 specialists have dual expertise in cardiology and neurology. Remarkably no specialist has expertise in all three areas. Furthermore, the number of specialists who have dual expertise in oncology and neurology equals the number of specialists who specialize exclusively in neurology.
TASK:
Are the events’ a specialist has expertise in cardiology and specialist has expertise in oncology independent? Justify your answer.
)   Are the events a specialist has expertise in oncology and a specialist has expertise in Neurology mutually exclusive? Justify your answer.
What is the probability that a randomly selected specialist has expertise in both oncology and cardiology?
)  What is the probability that a randomly selected specialist has expertise in either oncology or Neurology, but not both?

The tourism department of the city organised a boat race. Interested sailors participated in the competition, but some had never navigated the lake routes. The event manager described the course, starting the city harbor. One sailor travelled 6km due to North west to the lighthouse, then turned south and moved 4km to reach the Island and finally sailed at 20km/hr for 1.5 hours on bearing of 2700 to the beach.
Task;
(a)  As a geography student, Help the sailor describe the direction of the beach from the city harbor.           (b)  How much would the sailor save using the shortest route if each kilometre travelled cost UGX 2,500 from the city harbor?

Lugano owns a poultry farm with an existing rectangular enclosure that measures 12 meters in length and 8 meters in width. The farm has been growing rapidly, and due to an increased demand for chicken, he plans to expand the size of poultry enclosure. He intends to double the size of the existing enclosure by adding the same distance to both the length and width. To enclose the newly expanded area, he plans to install a new fence, with fence poles spaced 3 meters apart. The fencing material costs UGX 7,500 per meter, while each pole is priced priced at UGX 4,500. Lugano also requires one pole along the width to be placed directly in the centre of the enclosure, in order to meet the design specifications.
TASKS;
(a) Help Lugano determine the new dimensions of his poultry farms enclosure to accommodate the increased demand for chicken. How can he expand the current space while maintaining the required layout for his farm’s needs?                                                                                                                                                  (b) Create a detailed business expenditure sheet that calculates the total cost of fencing material and poles. How much will Lugano need to spend on new fencing and poles, and how should he plan for these expenses? Include all necessary calculations to determine the total budget for the expansion
